Ryujinx shader translator: room for NVN2's constant banks and storage buffers.
Ampere's constant bank field is 5 bits and NVN2 uses banks past Maxwell's 18: Fire Emblem Fortune's Weave's fragment
shaders read their push constants from c[0x18] (238 of 4,096 blocks), which overran the 18-entry slot map. The storage
buffer map grows to 32 as well (an NVN2 compute shader can reach 9 uniform blocks as storage plus 8 storage buffers; others
saw a kernel with 17 pointers). The harness's StaticGpuAccessor gives the new slots their own binding ranges. Applied at
build time by translator/Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader.csproj to a copy under the build folder. The Ryujinx code in the context
lines is MIT.
--- a/Translation/ResourceManager.cs
+++ b/Translation/ResourceManager.cs
@@ -65,8 +65,8 @@
             _stage = stage;
             _stagePrefix = GetShaderStagePrefix(stage);
 
-            _cbSlotToBindingMap = new SetBindingPair[18];
-            _sbSlotToBindingMap = new SetBindingPair[16];
+            _cbSlotToBindingMap = new SetBindingPair[32];
+            _sbSlotToBindingMap = new SetBindingPair[32];
             _cbSlotToBindingMap.AsSpan().Fill(new(-1, -1));
             _sbSlotToBindingMap.AsSpan().Fill(new(-1, -1));
 
